# shop_inch.machine — an inch-dialect controller (DECISIONS.md "K1 slice 1 —
# the formatting boundary…"). `units inch` flips the units word to G20 and
# converts every dimension word once at the formatting boundary; coordinate
# decimals default to 4 under inch (tenths of a thou), and `feed_decimals 2`
# is declared so the golden exercises the classes SPLIT — coordinates and
# feeds finally spell differently. `spindle_word` is left at its `decimal`
# default on purpose: the S words must come through the conversion untouched
# (an RPM has no length unit), which the twin test pins.
name Inch-dialect VMC
units inch
feed_decimals 2
